cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Health-Aware Closed-Loop Multi-Objective Scheduling for Warehouse AGV Fleets: Wall-Clock Evaluation and Reproducible Simulation"
authors:
  - family-names: Zou
    given-names: Yi
    affiliation: Zhanjiang University of Science and Technology
  - family-names: Mai
    given-names: Chunna
    affiliation: Zhanjiang University of Science and Technology
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/zouyi-0620/ehco-agv-scheduling"
abstract: >-
  Python reference implementation of the Equipment Health-Constrained
  Optimization (EHCO) framework: a four-layer closed-loop architecture coupling
  an AW-NSGA-II optimizer with a fuzzy-logic adaptive weight controller, a
  multi-indicator state-of-health model, and event-driven replanning for
  smart-warehouse AGV fleets. Includes the full experimental pipeline (E1
  static comparison, E2 component ablations, E4 dynamic closed-loop study with
  event-driven component ablation, E6 parameter sensitivity).
keywords:
  - AGV scheduling
  - closed-loop optimization
  - equipment health management
  - health-aware scheduling
  - multi-objective optimization
  - NSGA-II
  - warehouse automation
  - discrete-event simulation
  - smart warehouse
  - state of health
